Only \OUValidationLegacyGatePasses{} of the kinematically projected
surrogate runs satisfy
all legacy final-\SI{60}{s} thresholds; the remaining
\OUValidationLegacyGateFailures{} trigger at least one.  Those thresholds were
constructed as regression sentinels for the original deterministic realization,
not as population-level acceptance criteria.  The ensemble conclusions are
therefore based on the versioned raw metrics, paired differences, and intervals
rather than on the legacy pass/fail indicator.

